{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Decision Trees and Random Forests Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: Gini impurity and entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Build both split criteria from scratch and verify they agree on which splits are good."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import math"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def gini_impurity(labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if n == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    counts = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for label in labels:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        counts[label] = counts.get(label, 0) + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return 1.0 - sum((c / n) ** 2 for c in counts.values())"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def entropy(labels):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if n == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    counts = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for label in labels:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        counts[label] = counts.get(label, 0) + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return -sum("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (c / n) * math.log2(c / n) for c in counts.values() if c > 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: Find the best split"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Try every feature and every threshold. Return the one with the highest information gain."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def information_gain(parent_labels, left_labels, right_labels, criterion=\"gini\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    measure = gini_impurity if criterion == \"gini\" else entropy"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n = len(parent_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_left = len(left_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    n_right = len(right_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if n_left == 0 or n_right == 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return 0.0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    parent_impurity = measure(parent_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    child_impurity = ("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (n_left / n) * measure(left_labels) +"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        (n_right / n) * measure(right_labels)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return parent_impurity - child_impurity"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: Build the DecisionTree class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Recursive splitting, prediction, and feature importance tracking."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class DecisionTree:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, max_depth=None, min_samples_split=2,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 min_samples_leaf=1, criterion=\"gini\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 max_features=None):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_depth = max_depth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.min_samples_split = min_samples_split"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.min_samples_leaf = min_samples_leaf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.criterion = criterion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_features = max_features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tree = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.feature_importances_ = None"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_features = len(X[0])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.feature_importances_ = [0.0] * self.n_features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_samples = len(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.tree = self._build(X, y, depth=0)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        total = sum(self.feature_importances_)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if total > 0:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.feature_importances_ = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                fi / total for fi in self.feature_importances_"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [self._predict_one(x, self.tree) for x in X]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: Build the RandomForest class"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Bootstrap sampling, feature randomization, and majority voting."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "class RandomForest:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def __init__(self, n_trees=100, max_depth=None,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 min_samples_split=2, max_features=\"sqrt\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                 criterion=\"gini\"):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.n_trees = n_trees"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_depth = max_depth"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.min_samples_split = min_samples_split"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.max_features = max_features"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.criterion = criterion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        self.trees = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def fit(self, X, y):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n = len(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for _ in range(self.n_trees):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            indices = [random.randint(0, n - 1) for _ in range(n)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            X_boot = [X[i] for i in indices]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            y_boot = [y[i] for i in indices]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree = DecisionTree("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                max_depth=self.max_depth,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                min_samples_split=self.min_samples_split,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                max_features=self.max_features,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                criterion=self.criterion,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            tree.fit(X_boot, y_boot)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            self.trees.append(tree)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    def predict(self, X):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        all_preds = [tree.predict(X) for tree in self.trees]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        predictions = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for i in range(len(X)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            votes = {}"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            for preds in all_preds:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                v = preds[i]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                votes[v] = votes.get(v, 0) + 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            predictions.append(max(votes, key=votes.get))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return predictions"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "See `code/trees.py` for the complete implementation with all helper methods."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
